From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sit: pad request payloads to a multiple of 8

The vendor RIL pads the payload of every request it sends. Across 858
AP->CP requests in a capture from this baseband, every payload --
everything after the 12-byte request header -- is a multiple of 8 bytes
long, with no exceptions, while the header's `length` still declares the
true size. We sent the frame unpadded.

It is not a corner case: 55 SET_DATA_PROFILE frames per boot were shorter
than stock's, along with 0x0943, 0x0944 and the four AIMS stack ids. The
parity report counted SET_DATA_PROFILE as byte-identical only because it
compares the common prefix.

The CP reads `length` bytes, so the padding is invisible to it either way.
The point is to stop being the only thing on the bus that frames
differently, since every unexplained difference is one more thing to rule
out when the CP refuses something.

`length` is untouched: it already matches stock, because 8 + body_len is
12 + the true payload once the body's four reserved bytes are counted.
Header-only requests carry no body and are left alone -- stock's are 8
bytes and ours already match.
diff -ruN a/crates/samsung-sit-ffi/src/builders.rs b/crates/samsung-sit-ffi/src/builders.rs
--- a/crates/samsung-sit-ffi/src/builders.rs	2026-11-08 11:50:03.919412681 -0500
+++ b/crates/samsung-sit-ffi/src/builders.rs	2026-11-08 11:50:32.827914779 -0500
@@ -75,9 +75,36 @@
         .to_bytes()
         .expect("SIT header serialization is infallible");
     frame.extend_from_slice(body);
+    pad_payload(&mut frame, body.len());
     emit_bytes(frame, out, out_len)
 }
 
+/// The 4 bytes of `body` that land in the frame's reserved field, ahead of the
+/// payload proper.
+const RESERVED_SIZE: usize = 4;
+
+/// Pad the payload out to a multiple of 8, leaving `length` alone.
+///
+/// The vendor RIL does this to every request it sends. Across 858 AP->CP
+/// requests in a capture from this baseband, every payload -- everything after
+/// the 12-byte request header -- is a multiple of 8 bytes long, with no
+/// exceptions, while the header's `length` still declares the true size. We
+/// sent the frame unpadded, which left 55 SET_DATA_PROFILE frames per boot
+/// shorter than stock's, among others.
+///
+/// The CP reads `length` bytes, so the padding is invisible to it either way;
+/// the point is to stop being the only thing on the bus that does it
+/// differently. Header-only requests carry no body and are left alone --
+/// stock's are 8 bytes and ours already match.
+fn pad_payload(frame: &mut Vec<u8>, body_len: usize) {
+    if body_len <= RESERVED_SIZE {
+        return;
+    }
+    let payload = body_len - RESERVED_SIZE;
+    let pad = (8 - payload % 8) % 8;
+    frame.resize(frame.len() + pad, 0);
+}
+
 /// Build `GET_BASE_BAND_VERSION` (0x0901). The selector is mandatory; pass
 /// SAMSUNG_SIT_VERSION_ALL_FIELDS unless there is a reason not to.
 #[no_mangle]
